Third-party data
----------------

memproj/data/recipes_hummus.json is derived from HUMMUS, a linked recipe
dataset released for research use.

    "HUMMUS: A Linked, Healthiness-Aware, User-centered and
    Argument-Enabling Recipe Data Set for Recommendation."
    RecSys 2023.  https://doi.org/10.1145/3604915.3609491
    Source: https://gitlab.com/felix134/connected-recipe-data-set

The underlying recipe records were crawled from food.com and, per the
HUMMUS documentation, may be used for educational or scientific purposes
only. Commercial use is not granted by this repository.

This repository does NOT redistribute the HUMMUS source table. It ships
only a derived selection of 155 recipes (memproj/data/recipes_hummus.json)
used as a benchmark fixture -- recipe identifiers and ingredient lists
together with attributes derived by memproj/recipes.py. To rebuild the
catalogue from source, download the dataset from the URL above; the
source files are not included here and must not be committed to this
repository.

The HUMMUS reference code is distributed under GPLv3. No HUMMUS code is
included in this repository; this project only reads the dataset's tabular
data. The Apache-2.0 license above applies to the code in this repository
and does not alter the terms under which the underlying data may be used.

If you use the recipe catalogue, cite HUMMUS alongside this benchmark.
